Day 12
------

POLYMORPHISM -> One thing can have many forms

Shape-circle, square, triangle, rectangle.
water--vapour, ice burge.

we can achieve polymorphism using overloading  

method overloading - same method name different parameters. -or- Method overloading means having multiple methods with the same name in the same class, but with different parameter lists (different number, type, or order of parameters).


4 Rules are applicable
----------------------
1)Method names should be same
2)number of parameters should be different
3)Data type of parameters should be different
4)Order of parameters should be different

CONSTRUCTOR - constructor name should be same as the class name

Constructor Overloading

Constructor overloading means creating multiple constructors in the same class with different parameter lists.





Interview Questions
1. Can constructors be overloaded?

Yes. A class can have multiple constructors with different parameter lists.

2. Can methods be overloaded?

Yes. As long as their parameter lists differ.

3. Can constructors have a return type?

No. Constructors never have a return type, not even void.

4. Can constructors be inherited?

No. Constructors are not inherited.

5. Can constructors be static?

No. Constructors cannot be static.

6. Can methods be overloaded by changing only the return type?

No. The parameter list must change.



ENCAPSULATION ->wrapping up of data and methods in to single unit(class).

1)All variables should be private
2)For every method there should be 2 methods(get and set)
3)variables can be operated only through methods


Getter and Setter Methods in Java

Getter and Setter methods are used to access and modify private variables of a class.

